{
  // Nitro generates .output/server/wrangler.json on every build and merges this
  // file into it (nitro/dist/_presets.mjs: readWranglerConfig -> defu). Without
  // the routes below the generated config declares no routing at all, and
  // `npx wrangler deploy` - the deploy command on the production branch -
  // removes the Custom Domains that are not declared. That has already happened
  // once on this project: a deploy silently detached crm.giventakedevs.com and
  // deleted its DNS record.
  //
  // `name` is pinned for the same class of reason: without it nitro auto-derives
  // a worker name, so a rename of the directory or package would deploy to a
  // different Worker than the one serving traffic.
  "name": "callmesalem-giventake-studio",

  // Pinned on purpose. nitro leaves compatibilityDate at "latest", which
  // writes a recent date into the generated wrangler.json on every build - so
  // each rebuild silently opted into whatever runtime behaviour Cloudflare had
  // gated behind a newer date (a 2026-09-02 build got 2026-08-30, a 2026-09-09
  // build got 2026-09-06). This file wins over that default (defu in nitro's
  // cloudflare preset), so runtime behaviour now changes only when this line
  // does. Bump deliberately: edit it, run the build and `bun run smoke:worker`,
  // and review the change like code. scripts/worker-smoke.mjs refuses a build
  // whose emitted date differs from this one.
  "compatibility_date": "2026-09-06",
  "routes": [
    { "pattern": "giventakedevs.com", "custom_domain": true },
    { "pattern": "www.giventakedevs.com", "custom_domain": true },
    { "pattern": "crm.giventakedevs.com", "custom_domain": true },
  ],

  // Drives the campaign send tick. The cron reaches the engine through nitro's
  // `cloudflare:scheduled` hook (src/nitro/campaign-cron.ts) - a `scheduled()`
  // on src/server.ts would be stripped from the generated Worker, so BOTH this
  // trigger and that plugin are required for a single send to happen.
  //
  // Five minutes pairs with the runner's 300s claim lease: a tick that dies
  // mid-batch has its rows re-claimable by roughly the time the next one runs.
  // A duplicate claim is still safe - campaign_claim_step, not this schedule,
  // is what prevents a second send.
  "triggers": {
    "crons": ["*/5 * * * *"],
  },

  // Plain-text vars MUST live here, not only in the dashboard.
  //
  // Secrets survive a deploy because Cloudflare stores them separately, but
  // plain vars are part of the uploaded config: any `wrangler versions upload`
  // or `wrangler deploy` replaces them with whatever this file declares. On
  // 2026-08-21 a build dropped INTAKE_FROM_EMAIL that had been set in the
  // dashboard an hour earlier, which silently reverted the contact form to its
  // mailto fallback - `sendMail` returns "unconfigured" unless BOTH
  // RESEND_API_KEY and INTAKE_FROM_EMAIL are present (src/lib/intake.ts).
  //
  // Nothing secret belongs in this block; it is committed to the repo.
  // RESEND_API_KEY and the SUPABASE_* values stay as dashboard Secrets.
  "vars": {
    "INTAKE_FROM_EMAIL": "build@giventakedevs.com",

    // Where the lead notification is delivered. Without this the code falls back
    // to hello@giventakedevs.com (src/lib/intake.ts), which is not a mailbox
    // Salem reads - so notifications sent successfully and went nowhere.
    "INTAKE_TO_EMAIL": "build@giventakedevs.com",

    // Absolute origin for links that leave this Worker and are opened later,
    // elsewhere, by someone who never made a request to it. Today that is the
    // signing link in a signature-request email (src/server/documents/
    // deal-actions.ts): a relative path there is not a degraded link, it is a
    // dead one inside a contract, so an unset value REFUSES THE SEND rather
    // than mailing something useless. It is a plain value, so per the warning
    // above it belongs in this file - setting it only in the dashboard means
    // the next deploy drops it and signature sends start refusing again.
    //
    // The public site, not the CRM host: the signer is a client, not an
    // operator, and /sign/$token is deliberately unauthenticated.
    "SITE_BASE_URL": "https://giventakedevs.com",

    // The Perplexity MCP gateway (docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-24-perplexity-mcp-gateway-design.md).
    // Plain values, so they belong here. MCP_PERPLEXITY_KEY is a secret and stays
    // in the dashboard. MCP_OPERATOR_EMAIL is stamped on every decision Perplexity
    // records at Salem's direction; MCP_EXECUTE_HOURLY_LIMIT caps those per hour.
    "MCP_OPERATOR_EMAIL": "salem@giventakedevs.com",
    "MCP_EXECUTE_HOURLY_LIMIT": "20",

    // NOT YET SET - the send tick is a no-op until they are. CAMPAIGN_REPLY_TO
    // and CAMPAIGN_UNSUBSCRIBE_BASE are plain values, so per the warning above
    // they belong in this block: setting them only in the dashboard means the
    // next deploy drops them and the cron goes quiet again. Deliberately left
    // unset rather than guessed - the reply address must be one Cloudflare
    // Email Routing actually delivers to, or replies stop being detected and
    // the sequence keeps mailing someone who already answered.
    //
    //   "CAMPAIGN_REPLY_TO": "<a mailbox routed to this Worker>",
    //   "CAMPAIGN_UNSUBSCRIBE_BASE": "https://giventakedevs.com/api/unsubscribe",
    //
    // CAMPAIGN_TOKEN_SECRET, RESEND_API_KEY and the SUPABASE_* values are
    // secrets and stay in the dashboard, where a deploy cannot clear them.
  },
}
